{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 42, :comments ["<b>And I came today.</b> Today I set out and today I arrived — from here we learn that the earth contracted for him. Rabbi Acha said: the conversation of the servants of the fathers before the Omnipresent is finer than the Torah of the sons — for the section of Eliezer is doubled in the Torah, while many core principles of Torah were given only by allusion (Bereshit Rabbah)."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 24, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:00:14.699042733Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}